WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.068
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-All right, here we are,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.903
on Overtime, with the Executive
Vice President of the Center

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.204
for International Policy,
Matt Duss,

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.706
and the columnist
for<i> Tablet</i> magazine,
Jamie Kirchick.

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.708
Here are the things
people want to know.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:12.178
What explains
Israel's intelligence failure?

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.513
Yes, we never got to that.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.447
Why-- I mean-- Wow.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.884
I mean, Netanyahu
was always the security guy.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.352
I mean, people--
"Oh, he's an asshole,

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.287
but he's our asshole
and he's going to keep us safe

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.289
-and Israel was always--"
-MATT DUSS: Which was always
his main argument.

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:25.859
Yes, and always great
at this kind of stuff

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.927
and they have to be, they live
in the roughest neighborhood

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.028
in the world.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.897
How did this happen?
Great question.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.631
Well, I think
there was the operational level

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:36.436
where they took out
some sensors, right?

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.671
And somehow the Israelis
didn't see that.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:40.740
But I think there was a larger
strategic picture...

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:43.343 line:0%
-BILL MAHER: Has to be.
-...where they really did not
think that Hamas would

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.111 line:0%
attempt something like this.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.179 line:0%
-BILL: Well, they were--
-They thought that
Hamas was something-- Hamas--

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:48.715 line:0%
They could-- um,
could sort of deal with them

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:49.782 line:0%
in some way,
but that they would be so--

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:51.084 line:0%
BILL: They were letting in
guest workers.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.485
-They were letting in
guest workers...
-Right. They were-- They were...

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.453
...that Hamas would not be
so irrational or suicidal,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.689
whatever word you want to use,
to actually
perpetrate something.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.257
Yeah. I mean,
I would make two points here.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.460
One is just to understand
the scope of the intelligence

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.095 line:0%
failure here. We're talking
about-- I think it's some 1500

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.397 line:0%
Hamas fighters who were killed
inside Israel,

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.600 line:0%
you had probably
another 500 more

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.435 line:0%
who took the hostages
back into Gaza,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.670 line:0%
-so we're talking at least
2,000 people.
-BILL: Right.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.239
Um, that's a lot
of people talking.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.573
-BILL: To keep a secret?
-Um, that's a lot--

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.841
-Yes, exactly right.
-Right.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.443
The... the idea that
Israeli intelligence

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.945
could not figure this out

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.914
or know that something
was going on,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.715
but also the second point,
you know, I made reference

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.251
to this-- the settlements
to-- to Ben-Gvir.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.621
And Israeli security officials
and others have suggested

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.322
that one of the problems
that you had,

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:33.793
a lot of Israeli security
redeployed to the West Bank

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:37.296
to protect settler groups
for the purposes of promoting

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.699
settlements attacking
Palestinians and that left

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.034
the fence line
relatively undefended,

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.269
-which also suggests...
-BILL: Right.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.539
...that Hamas themselves
may have been shocked
at how easy it was

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.640
to cross the river.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:50.109
Also, I may say,
too many Jewish holidays.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.313
-(CHUCKLES)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.548
What? A lot of...

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.254
-I'm gonna let that one slide.
-A lot of the-- (CHUCKLES)

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.489
-BILL: A lot of the--
-MATT: As a-- as a Christian...

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.424
-A lot of the sol--
-...who got Jewish holidays,
I disagree.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.461
-I disagree.
-A lot of the soldiers were,
like, on leave.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:10.897
-And you know--
-JAMES KIRCHICK:
That was 50 years

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.665
to the day
of the Yom Kippur War.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.367
BILL: You think they would
see that coming.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.803
Yeah, it's like Lou Gehrig
and Lou Gehrig's disease, right?

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.138
-How didn't they know?
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.607
-What are the odds? (LAUGHS)
-JAMES: What are the odds?
(CHUCKLES)

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:22.941
(AUDIENCE CHEERS, APPLAUDS)

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:25.578
Okay, uh, well,
Ohio representative,

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:27.513
Jim Jordan... (LAUGHS)

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.082
This is-- This is hysterical,
