on specific humanitarian items.

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:47.259 line:0%
-BILL: So they say.
-So, it's not like
we're giving Iran--

00:08:47.325 --> 00:08:48.527
Under strict monitoring.

00:08:48.627 --> 00:08:49.728
-JAMES: But money is fungible.
-BILL: Yes.

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:51.631
Money is fungible,
and money that can go

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:54.666
to paying for humanitarian goods
can be also used on

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:55.901
-various purposes.
-No, but it's not as if--

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:58.704
And listen, as they say,
the military eats first, right?

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:01.339
So, Iran has not been--
even though they are under

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:03.375
some of the heaviest sanction
in the world,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.344
they still have not been,
you know,

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:08.180
they still have money to spend
on their military

00:09:08.246 --> 00:09:10.049
and all their, you know,
their nefarious activities.

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:12.651
This is just giving money
to actually help their people.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.252
Again,
not defending this regime.

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:16.488
No one should.
But, I think, let's understand

00:09:16.555 --> 00:09:17.556
the nature of this six billion

00:09:17.923 --> 00:09:19.358
-and what it was
gonna be used for.
-BILL: I got one last question.

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:22.361
I've been hearing a lot
this week that Nikki Haley

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:24.663
is really kicking ass,

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:27.799
that she's rising up
in the Republican Party.

00:09:27.866 --> 00:09:31.904
There she is. And, uh, I see
George Will's column says,

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:35.374
uh, Tim Scott should bow out
of the race, throw his support

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:36.976
to Nikki Haley,
encourage everybody else

00:09:37.042 --> 00:09:38.143
in the race
to do the same thing.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.145
That this
is the viable alternative

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:43.015
-to Donald Trump. And-- and...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:44.917
...and if we just had a race...

00:09:46.318 --> 00:09:49.321
If we just had a republican race
with just two people

00:09:49.521 --> 00:09:51.290
and Nikki Haley
was the alternative,

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:54.060
it's possible that she would
take it from Trump.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.461
There's a chance.
There's a chance.

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:57.463
And I thought she did great
in the first debate,

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:58.864
not as good
in the second debate.

00:09:59.198 --> 00:10:01.133
But, look, he has
over 50 percent

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:02.568
-Trump does.
-BILL: Now.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:05.604
-Now, and yeah--
-BILL: But if it was just
two people-- So there's--

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:07.639
Perhaps. She would have
a fighting chance, and yes,

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:09.708
I would absolutely--
that all the other

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:12.177 line:0%
Republicans running now,
need to do their patriotic duty

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.279 line:0%
and do what they didn't do
the last time

00:10:14.479 --> 00:10:17.883 line:0%
-and they need to rally behind
one anti-Trump alternative.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:20.152
-BILL: And she--
-Yeah, I don't know, we'll see--

00:10:21.754 --> 00:10:26.024
You know, if you remember,
you know, Trump has not really

00:10:26.091 --> 00:10:27.993
taken her on yet. He's waiting.

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:30.262
If you remember from,
you know,<i> Lord of the Rings,</i>

00:10:30.328 --> 00:10:32.731
-you know, the Eye of Sauron...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:10:32.865 --> 00:10:34.499
-MATT: Once the...
-I-- I don't.

00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:37.168
...Once the eye of Trump
turns to Nikki Haley,

00:10:37.302 --> 00:10:39.938
-with all its withering power--
(LAUGHS)
-I don't know movies like that.

00:10:40.005 --> 00:10:41.640
All right, thank you, guys.
I appreciate it.

00:10:41.707 --> 00:10:42.808
Thank you, everyone.

